WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.607
Endpoint and system telemetry provides activity that network observation may not reveal.

00:00:06.607 --> 00:00:17.618
Engineering workstations, HMIs, application servers, historians, jump hosts, and remote-access systems can record users, processes, files, services, configurations, and local events.

00:00:17.618 --> 00:00:24.715
Authentication records show successful and failed logons, account use, privilege, and session timing.

00:00:24.715 --> 00:00:31.811
File telemetry may reveal project access, new executables, configuration changes, or removable-media activity.

00:00:31.811 --> 00:00:39.886
Service events can identify startup, shutdown, failure, or changes to applications that support control visibility.

00:00:39.886 --> 00:00:48.451
Engineering workstations are especially important because specialized tools can configure controllers, HMIs, networks, and field devices.

00:00:48.451 --> 00:00:56.036
Relevant records may include project versions, downloads, connection targets, firmware work, and change approvals.

00:00:56.036 --> 00:01:00.686
These actions need strong identity and maintenance context.

00:01:00.686 --> 00:01:09.740
HMI, historian, and SCADA servers can provide alarms, application errors, tag changes, database activity, and collection health.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:20.751
Remote-access gateways add source, destination, approval, session duration, and sometimes activity records that connect an external identity to an internal asset.

00:01:20.751 --> 00:01:25.401
Collection must be compatible with the supported system.

00:01:25.401 --> 00:01:34.944
An endpoint agent, audit setting, or aggressive log forwarding configuration can consume resources or disrupt a legacy application.

00:01:34.944 --> 00:01:42.040
Test changes with engineering and vendors, monitor overhead, and define a rollback path.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:48.158
Normalize endpoint records with asset role, site, owner, and reliable time.

00:01:48.158 --> 00:01:54.275
Protect logs from unauthorized change and retain enough history for investigation.

00:01:54.275 --> 00:02:06.755
Cross-source correlation is strongest: a user logon, remote session, engineering connection, controller change, and process event together provide more confidence than any one record.
